{'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 7, 10, 10, 45, 43, 338522, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'task_id': '3e187d6c327c', 'workflow_id': '4c25dff055ea41f5', 'iteration': 1, 'files': [{'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 7, 10, 10, 45, 43, 338513, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'path': 'palindrome.py', 'content': 'import re\n\n\ndef is_palindrome(s: str) -> bool:\n    """\n    Check if a string is a palindrome, ignoring case, spaces, and punctuation.\n\n    Args:\n        s: The input string to check.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if the string is a palindrome after normalization, False otherwise.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> is_palindrome("A man, a plan, a canal: Panama")\n        True\n        >>> is_palindrome("race a car")\n        False\n        >>> is_palindrome(" ")\n        True\n    """\n    # Remove all non-alphanumeric characters and convert to lowercase\n    cleaned = re.sub(r\'[^a-zA-Z0-9]\', \'\', s).lower()\n    return cleaned == cleaned[::-1]\n\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    # Test cases\n    assert is_palindrome("A man, a plan, a canal: Panama") is True\n    assert is_palindrome("race a car") is False\n    assert is_palindrome(" ") is True\n    assert is_palindrome("Madam, I\'m Adam") is True\n    assert is_palindrome("No \'x\' in Nixon") is True\n    assert is_palindrome("Hello, World!") is False\n    assert is_palindrome("12321") is True\n    assert is_palindrome("123456") is False\n    print("All tests passed!")\n'}], 'explanation': 'The solution uses regex to remove all non-alphanumeric characters, converts to lowercase, then checks if the cleaned string equals its reverse. The file includes the function with type hints, a comprehensive docstring with examples, and 8 assert-based tests covering various edge cases including empty strings, punctuation, mixed case, and numeric palindromes.'}